{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 80,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle’s rapid deterioration from \nbeloved weekly staple to overpriced  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "slop bowl is one of the strangest corporate \nstories of the modern age. Just a decade ago,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9280,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the chain was a cornerstone of \nthe 21st-century American diet,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12880,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "known for generous portions, fresh \ningredients, lightning-fast service,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and stores packed with enthusiastic staff and \nloyal customers. If you needed a quick, healthy,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22400,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "affordable meal that could last for days between \nschool, work, or home, Chipotle had your back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27840,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was a company that genuinely seemed \nto take pride in not just what it served,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31520,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but also who it hired and the impact \nit had on the world around it. Today,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35600,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle is the opposite with undermanned \nstores filled with overworked employees  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40000,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "under pressure to give you the smallest \nportion possible off a stale, tired menu."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44880,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it's not because some executive randomly \ndecided to start serving less food. Instead,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49520,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what we're seeing today is the \nculmination of a 10-year-long  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52560,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pump and dump by a single Wall Street \nhedge fund - a play that netted them  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56400,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "$3 billion dollars and left everyone \nelse with tiny portions and worse food."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60560,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The rise and fall of Chipotle is a \ntimeless case study about politics,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64560,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "power, strategy, and the fundamental \ntradeoffs between founder idealism  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68800,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "versus investor pragmatism. \nIn this Modern MBA episode,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we dive into the economics and transformation \nof Chipotle through the decades and how a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77520,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wall Street hedge fund single-handedly fueled \nand crushed this once beloved Mexican chain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle and the entire fast casual market \nas we know today was created by McDonald’s,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87920,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wall Street, and the legacy fast \nfood industry. In the late 1990s,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92000,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "burgers had become saturated. Revenue had \nplateaued as there was a Wendy’s, McDonald’s,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96720,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or Burger King on every profitable corner in the \nUS. Americans literally could not eat any more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102000,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "burgers. Unable to simply open stores to grow, \nthese titans were under pressure to show upside."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107760,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the same time, a new rival had emerged, \ndelivering unprecedented growth and excitement.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112720,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yum Brands was on the ascent with a multi-brand \nportfolio. As the owner of Taco Bell, Pizza Hut,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118080,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and KFC, they scaled multiple categories \nsimultaneously to own all three meals of the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123040,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "day. If parents wanted pizza and kids wanted \ntacos, Yum Brands captured the entire sale.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128640,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was a similar dynamic abroad. In the late 80s, \nChina opened its doors to the West and became the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "single most valuable growth market for American \nfast food overnight. Yum Brands didn’t just beat  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "McDonald’s to China - they dominated them. \nFried chicken was an easier sell for Chinese  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144240,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consumers and the company outmaneuvered the \nGolden Arches in localization and operations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149520,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, the novelty of Taco Bell and \nPizza Hut captivated Americans back home.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154080,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While McDonald’s remained the stronger business,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156240,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yum Brands held greater momentum and potential. \nThe only way to grow in this emerging global fast  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161440,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "food war was for McDonald’s to assemble its \nown portfolio of brands and cuisines.By 2001,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167440,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "McDonald’s had acquired Boston Market to fight \nKFC, bought a Midwest pizza chain to fight Pizza  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172720,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hut, and invested in a tiny Denver Mexican \nchain called Chipotle to fight Taco Bell."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177840,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each move was aimed at chipping away at \nYum Brand’s dominance across Mexican,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181920,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pizza, and Chicken. Yet it was Mexican that \nheld the greatest potential. Since the 70s,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187120,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Taco Bell had introduced and normalized \nMexican cuisine, turning tacos, burritos,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192000,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and quesadillas into mainstream staples. They had \nproven demand and unit economics over decades. Yet  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198240,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for all its success, Taco Bell remained anchored \nto teens, college students, and single males."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the same time, the broader cultural shift \ntowards fitness and nutrition educated Americans  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208720,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to prioritize ingredient quality as \nmuch as portion control. By the 90s,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213280,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the business case for a higher-status, \nhigher-quality, Mexican chain was clear.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217760,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Taco Bell had made fortunes profitably selling \n$1 bean burritos and 60 cent tacos at scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223760,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The same model, upgraded with better \ningredients, could command three times  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227520,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the price and twice the profit. Startups like \nBaja Fresh and Chipotle emerged to fill this gap,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233440,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "replacing beef crumbles and processed \ncheese with real steak, fresh salsa,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and steamed rice. Ultimately, Mexican \ncuisine was more than just a trend."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241760,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the mid-2000s, McDonald’s was under fire \nfrom Western media and regulators for their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246640,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "role in the obesity epidemic. The unprecedented \nscrutiny upended the fast food burger business,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252080,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reshaping its existence from an essential \ntradition and into a public health liability  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256560,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like cigarettes. All this further elevated \nMexican cuisine as the superior, fresher,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262000,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "healthier, mass-market alternative and \nthe next big frontier for fast food."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "McDonald’s sunk hundreds of millions \nof dollars into Chipotle after its  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269760,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "initial investment - not just to hold \na stake in this fast-growing category,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273520,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but also to hedge against the increasingly \nfragile burger business. Their backing of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277600,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle set off an arms race as rivals raced to \nacquire Mexican chains and assemble multi-brand  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282960,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "portfolios of their own. Wendy’s shelled out over \na quarter of a billion dollars for Baja Fresh."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288480,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2002, it was the number one \nMexican fast-casual chain with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292080,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more stores than Chipotle. With no freezers \nand microwaves, they boasted a comprehensive,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296960,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "customizable menu that included \nfajitas, enchiladas, and shrimp."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301200,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this West Coast chain was not as \nscalable or bulletproof as advertised."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305360,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Despite its fast-casual branding,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Baja Fresh was really a conventional sit-down \nrestaurant where food was cooked to order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With high complexity and intensive labor, \nBaja Fresh was too inefficient to capture  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316160,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the throughput of a Chipotle, too cheap to capture \nthe margins needed to offset its cost structure,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321440,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and too expensive to drive the \nhabitual volume of a Taco Bell."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325120,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make matters worse, Wendy’s forced new Baja \nFresh stores into legacy drive-thru properties  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330480,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and refused to invest further, believing the \nconcept to be mature enough to sell itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335600,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, McDonald’s poured \ncapital to nurture Chipotle  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338640,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and secure the prime locations needed \nto reinforce its premium positioning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Starved and neglected, Baja Fresh crashed. \nAfter just 4 years, Wendy’s dumped the chain  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347760,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a fire sale for 30 million dollars, \na tenth of what it had initially paid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352240,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, Jack in the Box \nfound its horse in Qdoba."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355440,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Compared to Baja Fresh, it \nwas a far better business."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358320,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Qdoba was a copycat - its Denver-based \nfounders had witnessed the early success  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362640,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the first Chipotle in 1993 and \nreplicated its core blueprint,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367040,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the open kitchen to the \ncustomer-facing assembly line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370320,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first Qdoba opened up just miles \naway from the original Chipotle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374000,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They forced differentiation by offering the \nvery items that Chipotle refused to like queso,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381200,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nachos, soup and traded quality for variety."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382640,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was enough for the fast-growing brand to \nbe worth $45M in the eyes of Jack in the Box,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388000,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who leaned hard on franchising to drive expansion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But unlike McDonald’s, the company lacked the \nleverage and relationships for prime real estate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395920,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a result, Qdoba often ended up in lower-tier \nstrip malls, suburbs, and urban sites."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The franchisee model also made consistency \nimpossible as customer experience varied  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "store to store. Fundamentally, Qdoba and \nJack in the Box were simply too small."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411120,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They couldn’t match the resources or \ntalent of McDonald’s and Chipotle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414960,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As an inferior copycat, Qdoba \nremained a distant No.2 rather  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418960,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than a true competitor - even with \nthe promise of free guacamole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422800,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Jack in the Box eventually sold the Mexican \nchain for $300M in 2017 - having nonetheless  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "played a pivotal role in shaping the \nmodern fast-casual burrito market."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433360,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle’s success through the 2000s was not a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436000,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "case of simply having more \nmoney than everyone else."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438640,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While Jack in the Box and Wendy’s acted \nlike landlords maximizing returns from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442960,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their acquisitions, McDonald’s \nacted more like a silent partner."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446560,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even though they funded Chipotle's expansion \nand kept the chain afloat through losses,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450560,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Golden Arches allowed Steve Ells, Chipotle’s \nuncompromising founder to steer the ship."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455680,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet the relationship between founder \nand investor was contentious."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459280,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "McDonald’s pressured Chipotle to follow \nthe fast food playbook - add drive-thrus  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463440,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to increase volume, introduce fries \nto boost spend, redesign stores with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467680,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bright plastic and family seating, and \ndowngrade to the cheapest cuts of meat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471760,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a chef, Steve fought McDonald’s at every step."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474640,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was repulsed by frozen factory \nslop and refused to franchise."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478480,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle’s ruthlessly small menu was \ndriven more by personal conviction  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482080,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than hard math. It was the only way he \nbelieved high-quality ingredients could  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485840,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be delivered quickly, affordably, and at scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488800,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While its rivals sacrificed efficiency \nand quality in exchange for variety,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492720,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle’s streamlined model enabled \nthem to uniquely serve hundreds per hour."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497200,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This unprecedented combo of \nspeed, quality, consistency,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500560,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and value became Chipotle’s defining advantage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503440,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But even as Chipotle thrived \nthrough the mid-2000s,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506480,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was a tiny speck in McDonald’s empire."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For every $100 that the Golden Arches \ngrossed, only $3 came from burritos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514320,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for all the backlash over nutrition, \nMcDonald’s financials remained stable,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518400,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the stock on a clear path to recovery."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521040,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in the view of Bill Ackman, one \nof Wall Street’s present-day legends,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524720,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "McDonald’s stock had every reason to be higher."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527360,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In time, he would play both the hero \nand villain for Chipotle as the force  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who enabled its rise only to later wring \nout every bit of value for personal gain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536480,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for now, Ackman would be the hero. \nHe had been Wall Street’s golden boy - a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540800,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wonderkid who made his name during the \n90s hedge fund boom, shorting companies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545120,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He would tank their stocks by \nreleasing hundred-page research  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548080,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reports and waging public crusades \nagainst management in the press."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552000,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in 2003, his luck would run out as his hedge \nfund collapsed. By 2005, Ackman had re-emerged  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a new fund, Pershing Square. Seeking \nredemption, he set his sights on McDonald’s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563680,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the mid-2000s, McDonald’s was trading at around \n$30. Ackman borrowed billions and bet it all that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569840,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the share price would increase 50% within 2 \nyears. Since his position was built on options,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575360,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he needed the stock to go up fast \nand high enough to turn a profit. If  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579280,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "McDonald’s stock failed to surpass $40 by Year \n2, Pershing and Ackman would both be wiped out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585040,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With the clock ticking, Ackman had to \nforce a positive market reaction fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589040,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He went public with a 100 page presentation,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591760,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "asserting that the company was leaving billions \non the table and that shareholders deserved more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596320,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He demanded that McDonald’s spin off \nits real estate into a separate entity,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600000,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "borrow billions to fund share buybacks, and divest  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603040,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "non-core brands like Chipotle and Boston \nMarket to refocus exclusively on burgers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608320,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Despite their contentious relationship with Steve,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610640,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "McDonalds saw Chipotle as their high-growth \nasset of the future. But Ackman saw differently."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615760,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He argued that the Mexican chain was being held \nback. Chipotle would be far more successful and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620880,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "command a far higher valuation as a standalone, \nindependent business through its own IPO."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "McDonald’s, in turn, could liquidate its stake \nand return those proceeds to shareholders."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631200,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was all just financial engineering but Ackman’s  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633920,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "math was compelling enough \nto rally other shareholders."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637120,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He started assembling a coalition of investors \nand spreading awareness through the press."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641680,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "McDonald’s couldn’t ignore his \ndemands without risking a proxy war."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645200,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While they rejected his proposal on real \nestate, the Golden Arches quickly conceded  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649200,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the rest to appease shareholders and \nto sweep the story out of the news cycle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653680,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They agreed to re-franchise one thousand \nstores to lean further into real estate,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "increase share buybacks to 6 billion dollars, \nand to spin off the non-burger brands."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662800,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle’s IPO turned McDonald’s $350  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666000,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "million dollar investment into \na $1.1 billion dollar windfall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670080,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These measures fueled a massive bull run, doubling \nMcDonald’s share price to over $60 by 2007."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676800,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "McDonald’s exited the fast casual market, Steve \nregained full control of the company he founded,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681920,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Ackman closed out his position to \nwalk away with $500 million in profit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687040,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now independent, Chipotle \nreturned to its founder-led model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690320,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From 2006 to 2010, Steve worked to \nshed McDonald’s past influence and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695360,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ingrain the unorthodox philosophy that had \nmade the chain successful in the first place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700160,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steve adopted an unconventional co-CEO \nstructure, where he focused on supply chain  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and product while his childhood friend Monty \nMoran took charge of staffing and operations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709360,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like before, he dismissed the constant \nshareholder calls for standard restaurant  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713040,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "industry tactics like limited-time \noffers, promotions, and menu expansion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717440,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, he and Monty refined the core system, \nequipment, and worker roles to push throughput."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723120,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tortillas were now warmed in seconds, dedicated \nexpedite-ers handled bagging, cashiers focused on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728320,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "payment, and a single cook in the back restocked \nso that the assembly line never stopped moving."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733120,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet Steve and Monty were also \nmindful of workers as humans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736800,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They treated Chipotle as a vehicle for change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739360,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The company introduced unprecedented \nsix-figure compensation packages for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743280,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "top-performing managers, cut ties with \nindustrial farms to reduce pollution,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747680,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "removed GMOs from its supply chain, championed \nmentorship over micromanagement, and required  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752960,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a minimum percent of ingredients to be sourced \nfrom small farms to lower its carbon footprint."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758080,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While the chain had expanded \naggressively under McDonald’s,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760960,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steve hit the brakes asserting that talent, \nnot capital, was the real constraint."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765200,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle would now only open as many \nstores as it had good people to run them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769360,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Managers were evaluated less on profit and more \non leadership, team cohesion, and employee morale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775600,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stores with lower revenue but stronger \nstaff camaraderie, higher energy,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779760,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and better retention were favored over those \nwith better sales and stressed environments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784560,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Workers were promoted based on their soft skills \nas much as performance. It was a simple belief  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789440,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of inputs and outputs - happy employees produce \nfaster lines, better food, and loyal customers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795840,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even as spending slowed during the Great \nRecession, Chipotle reached new heights."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800000,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With industry leading restaurant-level \nmargins, the company demonstrated that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803680,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the costs of premium ingredients, intensive labor, \ngenerous portions, and direct ownership over every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809520,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "store could be offset by radical efficiency, \nsheer volume, and genuine customer loyalty."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 815280,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From 2010 to 2014, Chipotle \nwould enter its golden age."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819760,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The stock in this period soared from 200 dollars \nto 800, outperforming the S\u0026P500 by 4 times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826400,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their valuation multiples exceeded even their \nformer parent, McDonald’s at its historical peaks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831920,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On a per-store basis, the average \nChipotle was grossing more than most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835680,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the fast food brands and netting \nhigher margins than steakhouses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839520,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Investors saw Chipotle not as a \nfast-growing restaurant chain,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842800,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as a disruptive, blue-chip, consumer \ntech business on par with Netflix and Amazon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848320,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Under Steve, the company had \nspent virtually nothing on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 851040,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mass advertising and was only at a \nfraction of the scale of Taco Bell."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854880,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The majority of restaurants were concentrated in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just 10 states with no presence in the \nDeep South, Great Plains, and overseas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862400,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle looked poised to disrupt not just \nfast food, but the entire restaurant industry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867200,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With results like these, few could question Steve."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870080,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was revered for seeing \na future two decades ahead  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872560,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of anyone else and sticking \nto it when no one believed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875600,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He continued to double down on values over \nconvention, removing carnitas rather than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879920,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compromise on animal welfare, refusing trends \nlike ordering kiosks and table tablets,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884800,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "underpricing the menu to maintain \naccessibility nationwide, and vetoing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888800,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "annual price hikes - insisting that prices should \nonly rise when justified by better ingredients."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894240,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brown rice, chips, and sofritas \nbecame new core additions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898160,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stores got new grills that \ncould cook multiple items  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900800,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simultaneously for better sear and faster output."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903840,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle was among the first restaurants  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905520,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to launch a mobile app as a way \nto relieve the in-store lines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908880,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steve wasn’t resistant to change \n- rather, he simply filtered every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912480,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "possibility under a single lens: it had \nto improve either throughput or quality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 917440,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle’s success ignited \na fast-casual gold rush as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920560,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "investors and operators rushed to replicate \nthis seemingly perfect business model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924800,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Blaze applied the format to pizza and was quickly \nfollowed by a wave of clones like mod, Pie-ology,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and PizzaRev. Sweetgreen extended the model \nto salads and even higher price points."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 935440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, Kahva and Zoe’s Kitchen replicated \nChipotle for Mediterranean cuisine,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940240,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "positioning themselves as fresher, \ncolorful, modern alternatives."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944160,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All these new entrants were backed \nby venture capital, private equity,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947680,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or the legacy fast food chains who were \nincreasingly worried about being left behind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952240,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The surge of Shake Shack along with failed \nhealthy pivots by legacy fast food giants  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956480,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through the mid-2010s demonstrated \nthat Americans were willing to pay  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960080,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more for higher-quality fast-casual \nfood and to do so through new brands."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964480,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The rapid emergence of new entrants meant \nthat Chipotle was now simply the new baseline."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 969120,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because all these concepts \ntargeted the same demographic of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 972160,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "urban professionals and millennials, they \nwere all competing for the same real estate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 976640,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Before, Chipotle only needed \nto outbid Subway, Starbucks,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979920,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or Panera Bread. Now, it was facing dozens of \nthese cross-category imitators for the same space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 985520,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For Steve, Chipotle was not about Mexican food, \nbut instead a repeatable formula of real estate,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990880,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "operations, supply chain, and culture \nthat could be applied to any cuisine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995600,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While they couldn’t compete everywhere,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 997200,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they also couldn’t afford to let these \nstartups sweep the market entirely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000880,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steve went on the offensive with ShopHouse as \na first mover in Asian cuisine - a category  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1005920,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "long defined by fried foods, frozen \ningredients, and heavy sugary sauces."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010720,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On defense, he launched Pizzeria Locale,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1013200,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aiming to replicate wood-fired pies \nat a fraction of the time and cost."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016960,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These new ventures reinforced Chipotle’s narrative  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019440,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to investors that they were a platform \ncompany rather than a Mexican chain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now a decade later, most of this fast-casual \nboom turned out to be a false gold rush. What  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028240,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was once hailed as long-term disruption \nultimately proved to be short-term hype."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032880,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today, Blaze has shifted to franchising \nto survive, Mod is shuttering nationwide,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1037600,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pie-ology is bankrupt, and PizzaRev \nhas vanished - while the old-school  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "giants of Domino’s, Pizza Hut, and \nPapa John’s continue to thrive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1046480,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sweetgreen has never been profitable \nat any point in its 19-year history  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1050320,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and continues to lose hundreds of \nmillions of dollars every year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The demand for $20 salad bowls evaporated \nwith the rise of remote work, inflation,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058400,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and economic slowdown."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060080,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Zoe’s Kitchen crashed under \nplummeting sales and its  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1062720,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "real estate was harvested by its closest rival."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1065520,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kahva remains the lone survivor, but \neven they have only sustained through  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "constant menu innovation, suburban \nexpansion, and minimal price hikes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073760,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Chipotle operating model would prove to be far  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1076240,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the silver bullet that Steve and \nmany others dreamed of at the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1079920,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet none of this was visible \nin the context of 2011 to 2015."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084320,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "During this Golden Age, Chipotle was the \nmarket maker, the model everyone copied,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1088400,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the stock everyone wanted to own."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1090400,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their breakout drew the attention of a bitter  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1092720,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bill Ackman, now 8 years removed \nfrom Chipotle’s initial spinoff."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1096560,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He had exited McDonald’s far too early, \nselling all his shares just before  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1100320,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Golden Arches entered a multi-year \nrally that ultimately tripled the stock."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1104480,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman had left literal billions on \nthe table. He had instead redirected  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1108640,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the profits from McDonald's to fund \nan activist turnaround at Burger King."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112560,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what was supposed to be a simple deal \nturned into a grueling fight bogged down  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116560,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with private equity, cost-cutting, messy \nfranchisee battles, and expensive marketing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1121760,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pershing Square exited Burger King with \nover a billion in profit but in hindsight,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1126240,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "riding Chipotle’s ascent would have \nbeen easier, faster, and more lucrative."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1130320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet Pershing Square was not a mutual fund that \ncould simply ride the market like a passenger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134880,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a hedge fund, it needed to \ngenerate alpha to justify its fees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138800,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman needed a reason to invest \nin Chipotle - some credible case  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142320,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the company was mismanaged, underperforming,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or inefficient - something that could \njustify Pershing's position and activism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1149440,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there was no such argument. Investors \nwere ecstatic with their 3000% returns."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1154560,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If anything, Chipotle was \novervalued, not undervalued."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1157920,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It had become one of America’s most \nadmired companies and Steve was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1161600,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "idolized as a culinary prophet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1163520,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Beyond the pace of expansion, there \nwas no real operational weakness,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1166960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no material shareholder dissatisfaction, \nand thus, no cause for intervention."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171520,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet just one year later, a black swan event would \nstrike, creating the generational opening for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1176400,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman to not only pounce, but also alter the \nstructure and direction of Chipotle forever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1182560,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’ve covered a wide range of \ntopics on Modern MBA — from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1185600,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nightclubs and barbershops \nto cookies and bubble tea."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1188400,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We manually parse financials, focusing \nnot just on revenue and profit,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1192160,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but on the key metrics that reveal how each \nindustry and business actually performs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1196800,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This rigor is why Modern MBA videos \nare used in university classrooms,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1201120,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from UC Davis to Denver. Because data \nintegrity and original insight are core  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1205760,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to what we do, we’ve always been skeptical of AI."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every AI tool hallucinates numbers, quotes \nincorrect headlines from questionable sources,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1213120,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and blindly confirms whatever you want to believe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1215520,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over the years, we’ve built an internal \ndatabase — a vault of curated financials  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1219680,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and verified operating metrics \nacross dozens of industries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1223120,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But even though we have the most \nreliable data, it’s been impossible  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1226080,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to actually use it altogether. If we \nwant to analyze across industries,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1229760,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we have to navigate thousands of cells, \nstitch formulas across hundreds of tabs,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1234240,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then manually reconcile the \nfindings with the latest earnings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1237680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s tens of hours for a single query which is \nwhy we’ve never attempted it in the first place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1242640,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we upload these sheets to Claude, it would \nbe the same problem - we’d have to download,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1246800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "upload, explain, wait, and then repeat \nit all over whenever we collect new data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1251840,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For years, we couldn’t find a way to integrate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1253840,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "AI into our workflow to improve \nquality - until now with Zapier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1257760,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With Zapier, cross-industry real-time \nanalysis is finally achievable!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1262000,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can ask questions of our own \ndata-set in simple English like:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1265600,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is the restaurant or retail industry \nstructurally more profitable than fashion?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1277120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What is the worst business ever covered \non Modern MBA — is it oat milk, GoPro,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1281840,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "BuzzFeed, esports, scooters \n— or something even worse?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1287280,
    "dDurationMs": 11280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or my favorite - how many modern Pokémon \ncards and what exact kind and condition  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1298560,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would you need to sell in a year just \nto gross as much as a single Taco Bell?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1302480,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Through Zapier, Claude securely \naccesses our internal vault,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1305760,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eliminating hallucinations and guesswork entirely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1308560,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Zapier MCP integrates everything into a single \nworkflow: instead of manually prompting Claude  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1313920,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every time, we just say, “run a full analysis,” \nand get answers grounded in our own trusted data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1318960,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet where Zapier shines is that \nit automatically injects live  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1322160,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "context from recent news about the \nexact companies we’ve asked about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1325920,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means all findings get \nautomatically pressure-tested  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328800,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to see if these past business patterns are \nstill holding or are starting to break."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1332960,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s been awesome seeing Zapier unlock value  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1335360,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that simply wasn’t possible and \nbetter the quality of our work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1338640,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Future analysts at our company can \nsecurely access the Modern MBA vault  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1342320,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to collect the findings without getting \nbogged down in the raw spreadsheets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1346000,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our MCP is built with Google Sheets, Google Drive,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1348480,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and WebSearch as that’s just what we use today, \nbut if the team starts using Slack or Airtable,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1353600,
    "dDurationMs": 4535,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can simply add those steps in as \nZapier today supports over 9,000 apps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358135,
    "dDurationMs": 52,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The best part is that this \nsetup took just minutes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358187,
    "dDurationMs": 74,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Credentials are handled through OAuth \nand we never expose our data or API  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358261,
    "dDurationMs": 62,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "keys to Claude. We didn't need \nto write a single line of code  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358323,
    "dDurationMs": 77,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or go spelunking through documentation. \nEverything was click, drag, and drop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358400,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you’re tired of trying to squeeze value out of \nisolated AI tools and want to actually bend AI to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1363920,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fit into your existing workflows, rather than the \nother way around, Zapier is that missing piece."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1369200,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Go to our special link in the \ndescription to get started with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1371920,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any one of Zapier’s ready-to-go templates \nand get real plug-and-play results from AI."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1376800,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you to Zapier for supporting Modern \nMBA and making this episode possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1382960,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The company would enter its fourth \nand most transformative era in 2015."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1387360,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It started in Minnesota, where 64 people came \ndown with salmonella after eating at Chipotle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1392800,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A month later, more than 200 customers in \nLos Angeles contracted norovirus after a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1397440,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sick manager was allowed to work, resulting in one  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1399760,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the largest single-restaurant \noutbreaks in American history."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1402960,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet the real hammer would drop just \n2 months after when 60 people came  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1406400,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down with e-coli after eating \nat Chipotles across 11 states."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1410480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then just weeks later after that, more than 100 \npeople, including an entire college basketball  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1415520,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "team, came down with norovirus in Boston \nafter another sick employee showed up to work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1420800,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steve made a public apology on the Today \nShow but no one could stop the fallout."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1425360,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The persistence, frequency, and \nscale of these incidents was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1428720,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unprecedented. This was not just a PR disaster,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1431440,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but a genuine public health crisis that no \ncompany statement could sweep under the rug."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1436080,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The CDC, FDA, and Department \nof Justice quickly launched  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1439760,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a criminal investigation into the company."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1442160,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the end of the year, few \ndared to eat at Chipotle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1445040,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In less than 6 months, Chipotle had \nsuffered five separate outbreaks,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1448640,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sickening over 500 customers across 14 states \nand involving 3 completely different pathogens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1454480,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was a black swan event - unpredictable,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1457040,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "massively consequential, and \nonly explainable in hindsight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1460480,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even the deadliest food safety disasters \nin American history had been isolated to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1464800,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "single events and single batches. \nThey never cascaded like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1468560,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sales and consumer trust \nevaporated almost overnight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1471840,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The stock dropped over 35% in a single \nmonth and would continue to free-fall  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1476080,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a 70% decline a year later, wiping out \nnearly all the gains of the Golden Age."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1481360,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The sheer improbability of the entire \nsituation and the rapid reversal of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1485600,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fortunes triggered conspiracies amongst \ninvestors - perhaps this was the result  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1489920,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of sabotage from short sellers, \nGMO lobbyists, or even McDonald’s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1494880,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in reality, there was a simpler explanation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1497600,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In pursuit of local, sustainable, \nand ethical ingredients,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1500800,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steve had decentralized Chipotle’s \nsupply chain during the Golden Age,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1504480,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shifting away from big conglomerates \nand towards small regional farms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1508400,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These small farms didn’t have the record-keeping  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1510720,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rigor and traceability technology \nas the big industrial suppliers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1514960,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a result, neither Chipotle nor \nthe CDC were able to ever determine  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1519200,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exactly what ingredient caused all these \noutbreaks and which farm it came from."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1523200,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steve’s commitment to freshness was also at fault."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1525840,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Despite scaling to thousands of locations, \nall the produce was still being washed,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1530080,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chopped, and prepared by hand at each store."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1532800,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This meant that food safety rested on the daily \ndiscipline and execution of Chipotle’s 60,000  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1538080,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hourly workers - and all it took was a single \nemployee to slip up, for bacteria to spread."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1543360,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With a crisis on their hands, \nSteve and Monty moved rapidly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1546640,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to re-industrialize the supply \nchain with new safety protocols."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1550400,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Barcode traceability was mandated on \nevery shipment of meat and produce."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1554800,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steak was no longer grilled from raw at every \nstore, but instead pre-cooked in sous-vide bags."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1560320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tomatoes and cilantro were now sanitized \nand diced in central kitchens before being  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1564880,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shipped to every store. And every \ningredient got tested for pathogens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1569040,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The sudden collapse in demand also \nforced cost discipline downstream."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1573040,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With customers no longer \nautomatically walking in the door,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1576000,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "food safety and P\u0026L became hard \nrequirements for store managers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1580240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Good vibes and happy staff were \nno longer enough to get promoted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1583760,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, nearly all the \npositive momentum was wiped out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1586960,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The launch of chorizo as a new meat, the \nexpansion of ShopHouse and Pizzeria Locale,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1591680,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even the rollout of a rewards program were \nall overshadowed by the food safety crisis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1596800,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just as Chipotle was projecting this \ntotal commitment to rebuilding trust,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1600640,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the company’s CMO was suddenly \narrested in a NYPD drug bust."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1605200,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He had been caught on wiretaps arranging  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1607120,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "monthly cocaine deliveries to his \napartment for nearly half a year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1610720,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The optics were as ironic as they were disastrous."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1613760,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The executive had been friends \nwith Steve and Monty since college."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1617200,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even after his indictment, Steve refused to fire  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1619760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "his longtime friend and even reinstated \nhim less than 3 months after his arrest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1624400,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Shareholders began to question Steve’s \njudgement and his prioritization of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1628160,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "friendships over business. The situation \nonly added to the growing perception  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1632320,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Chipotle was an old boy’s club \nrather than a disciplined company."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1636160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the same time, despite tens \nof billions of lost market value,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1639760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steve and Monty each remained some \nof the highest paid CEOs in America."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1644400,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were each paid the equivalent \nof a full CEO salary, with individual  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1648400,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compensation packages that surpassed what \nTim Cook, Jensen Huang, Howard Schultz,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1653280,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Reed Hastings, and other famous \nCEOs were making at the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1656880,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Despite splitting responsibilities \nbetween operations and food,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1660240,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they had each objectively failed \nin their assigned domains."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1675920,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This only spiked labor costs and \nwiped out the stellar margins that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1679200,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had fueled Chipotle’s valuation \nin the first place. These moves  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1682560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all felt less like strategy and more \nlike rash, emotional, panic reactions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1687200,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It didn’t help that Steve declined to make any \nfurther media appearances after his apology  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1691600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the Today Show. His reluctance to engage \npublicly forced the company to lean on cold,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1696800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "impersonal, and rehearsed press releases \nthat did nothing to reassure customers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1701840,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Disgruntled investors increasingly \ndirected their anger at the board,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1705360,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which appeared to be another \nold boy’s club who were more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1708000,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interested in rubber-stamping Steve’s \npaychecks than holding him accountable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1711760,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With the stock down by more \nthan 50% and increasingly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1714720,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "restless shareholders, Ackman pounced."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1717200,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pershing sunk over a billion dollars in \nChipotle, acquiring 9.9% of the company."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1722320,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At this stage, Ackman was a living Wall Street  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1724560,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "legend who had left a trail \nof bodies wherever he went."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1727680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since his campaign against McDonald’s \nin 2007, he had deposed 9 different CEOs  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1732640,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and reshaped industries from railroad \nand pharma to fashion and bookstores."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1737360,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He and his hedge fund were coming \noff a catastrophic loss that had  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1740560,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "his own shareholders stunned and \nerased much of his earlier gains."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1744400,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman was desperate for a win and \nburritos looked simple in comparison."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1748720,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle immediately went on the defensive,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1750960,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hiring banks and lawyers to try and \nprevent Ackman from buying more shares."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1754960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Publicly, Steve gave Pershing Square the cold \nshoulder. He saw Ackman as a corporate raider  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1759440,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the exact kind of short-term mentality \nhe had spent the past decade fighting against."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1763840,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it was all futile."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1765120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wall Street, like Silicon Valley, runs on \nsoft power - and Ackman had no shortage of it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1769840,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He didn’t need to own 51% \nof Chipotle to take control."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1773360,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, he simply needed to rally \nother shareholders to his side."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1778560,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If enough institutions aligned behind Ackman, \nthey could collectively vote out the existing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1783040,
    "dDurationMs": 5208,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "board and management, including Steve, and put in \ntheir own hand-picked leaders to run the company."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1788248,
    "dDurationMs": 72,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By 2016, more than 95% of Chipotle's \nshares were owned by institutions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1788320,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All Ackman needed was to flip the biggest ones \nonto his side - Vanguard, BlackRock, and Fidelity  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1793840,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and convince them that he had a better plan to \nsave the company than Steve and his college pals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1799040,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These three index funds combined \nheld roughly 30% of Chipotle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1803120,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Behind the scenes, they had begun \nsouring on Steve amid the stock's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1806320,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "multi-billion dollar collapse, \nlooming criminal investigation,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1809840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and ongoing embarrassment surrounding \nits CMO - who still somehow had a job."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1814720,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Below these giants sat hundreds of smaller \ninstitutional investors like endowments  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1819040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and pension funds, each holding less than a \npercent of Chipotle yet had far more to lose."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1824240,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For them, every dollar lost in Chipotle \nwas a dollar less for their unions.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1828320,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These losses could not be swept under the \nrug the same way they could at index funds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1832800,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman became the spearhead for \nall these disgruntled institutions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1836480,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They could quietly support him behind-the-scenes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1838720,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while he waged the public war that \nthey could not pull off themselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1842320,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So while Steve and Monty had their hands full \njust trying to keep Chipotle from unraveling,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1847040,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman was working full-time to build this \ncoalition - holding private conversations,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1851840,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flipping shareholders to his side, and \nturning sentiment against management."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1855840,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If Chipotle was to go to war against \nPershing, it would be a humiliating,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1859680,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "drawn-out, public affair - one that Ackman \nwould win every time in a landslide. It  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1864240,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would also be a distraction that \nthe business could not afford."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1867440,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, Chipotle had no choice but to settle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1869840,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman was granted four board seats \nthat he then filled with his own people."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1874000,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The company accepted his demands to fire Monty \nand permanently abolish the co-CEO structure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1879280,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In exchange, Ackman agreed not to publicly \ncriticize Chipotle or launch a hostile takeover."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1884480,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With Pershing's enforcers \nnow inside the boardroom,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1886880,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the company's priorities changed overnight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1889360,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman's vision was that Chipotle \ndidn’t need to invent new things,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1892720,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it simply needed to make the \nexisting product easier to buy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1896080,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While Steve believed seeing workers scoop \nfood was part of the customer experience  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1900000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that digital ordering would forever \nbe a supplement to the in-store business,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1904000,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman saw it as the complete opposite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1906480,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For him, digital was the low-hanging fruit that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1908960,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would materially grow revenue and profits \nas the primary sales channel of the future."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1913600,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By pushing more customers onto the app, \nChipotle could install a second assembly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1917440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "line inside every restaurant dedicated \nexclusively to fulfilling online orders."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1922240,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead of having to double \nthe size of the store or staff,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1925200,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each location could now process \ntwice as many orders simultaneously."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1929200,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the same time, the digital line would \nremove the system’s biggest bottleneck,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1932880,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which were the customers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1934000,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Workers would no longer need to wait on people \nto make their selections or ask questions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1938560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This line would be inherently optimized for \nnot just speed and efficiency, but also profit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1943360,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For in-store customers watching every \nscoop of rice, cheese, meat, or guacamole,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1948560,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "workers generally gave out larger portions to \navoid confrontation and to keep the line moving."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1953680,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But on digital orders, there was no customer \npresent to haggle over portions. Employees  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1958080,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could now follow exact corporate serving \nspecifications with far greater consistency."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1962720,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a result, the exact same burrito \nordered online would carry a lower  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1966720,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "food cost and net higher profit \nthan one ordered in person."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1970320,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At scale, every fraction of protein removed \nfrom millions of bowls and burritos across  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1975120,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thousands of stores would quietly flow \nstraight back into Chipotle’s margin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1979440,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus, to Ackman, digital was \nlow-hanging fruit that Steve  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1982320,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had stubbornly and needlessly resisted for years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1985120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In his view, Steve was too ideological to \nbe an effective CEO. He was wasting time  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1990240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and money chasing marginally better \ningredients when the foundations of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1993760,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a far more profitable business were \nalready sitting in front of him."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1997360,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now with direct influence inside the company, \nAckman's recommendations turned into mandates,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2002240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and digital ordering quickly \nbecame the company's new obsession."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2005760,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The old emphasis on culture \nwas replaced with hard,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2008480,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "immediate financial targets as Steve \npublicly committed to cutting $100  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2012560,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "million dollars in cost and hitting \nan earnings per share of ten dollars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2016480,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was just one of Ackman’s many signals \nfrom behind-the-scenes that Chipotle,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2020560,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "under his watch, would now finally \nprioritize profits over ideology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2025280,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By mid-2017, Chipotle appeared \nto be emerging from the crisis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2029600,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sales had slowly rebounded. The \nhigher-margin digital channel surged  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2033520,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the company rolled out incentives \nfor app signups and mobile orders."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2037680,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every store was now equipped with \na secondary digital make line. For  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2041200,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the first time in 3 years, the chain \nfelt confident enough to raise prices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2045440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The maligned CMO returned to work \nand Steve remained in the kitchen,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2049760,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "developing new menu items like queso, margaritas, \nand tortilla desserts to re-excite customers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2055920,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It had been 19 months since the \nlast incident. No new outbreaks had  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2059760,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "occurred. His supply chain reforms and new \nmanagement protocols seemed to be working."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2064080,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By every measurable metric, \nthe turnaround was working."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2067200,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Investor confidence slowly returned as Ackman \ncontinued reshaping Chipotle into a disciplined,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2072560,
    "dDurationMs": 1476,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "numbers-driven machine. His influence \nat this point was so strong that he  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2074036,
    "dDurationMs": 204,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was hiring fast food veterans directly into \nthe executive ranks over Steve's objections."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2074240,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything was going smoothly until July,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2076480,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when a norovirus outbreak at a single store \nin Virginia sickened over 100 customers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2081920,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was discovered that once again, \na sick employee had been allowed to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2085200,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "work despite Steve's new zero-tolerance policies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2088400,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The incident immediately reignited \nthe ‘Chipotle is unsafe’ narrative,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2092000,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "undoing much of the hard-earned trust the \ncompany had spent the past year rebuilding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2096160,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Within hours, the stock collapsed. \nInvestors were baffled at how this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2100000,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could keep happening while customers feared \nit as the start of another food safety crisis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2104400,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like any good activist, Ackman would \nnot let this crisis go to waste."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2108640,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steve had made progress, but not at \nthe speed, urgency, and scale needed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2112720,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was also not an obedient, loyal,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2114880,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "executioner who was willing to fully embrace \nAckman’s digital, data, and profit-first model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2120640,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Virginia outbreak and \nensuing stock selloff had  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2123360,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "made the situation untenable for Pershing Square."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2126080,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Despite 18 months of intervention, \nChipotle's shares were still trading  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2129680,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "below the hedge fund's entry point. \nPershing Square was now in the red  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2133200,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a third consecutive year. For his own \nshareholders, Ackman needed results and fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2138160,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With the board now firmly under his control,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2140400,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he mobilized quickly behind \nthe scenes for a regime change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2144000,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In reality, the Virginia outbreak was \nvery different from the 2015 crisis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2148240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was an isolated incident caused \nby human error rather than the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2151760,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "systemic supply chain failures of the \npast. And from a pathogen standpoint,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2156240,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "norovirus outbreaks are relatively common and \noccur every year in the restaurant industry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2161520,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Steve’s food safety protocols had worked \nand they still remain in effect to this day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2166160,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman weaponized the Virginia outbreak as an \nexcuse to boot Steve out of his own company.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2170880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He argued that Steve had been given 18 months, \nunlimited resources, boardroom support,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2175840,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and continuous executive help - yet people \nwere still getting sick eating Chipotle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2180480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In short, Steve was framed as the problem - \na founder who was too emotional, dogmatic,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2185680,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and stubborn to adapt and evolve with the company."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2188560,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman did not personally wield the \nknife, but he certainly sharpened it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2192080,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No one ever came to Steve’s defense and the board \nlet all the criticism, panic, and controversy fall  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2197120,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on his shoulders. It's likely that Ackman, with \nall his media connections, quietly amplified  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2202000,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Virginia incident in the news in order to \njustify the regime change behind closed doors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2207600,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The reality was that Ackman had \nalready found his guy - he just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2210880,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "needed the opportunity and excuse to depose Steve."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2213920,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Less than three months after \nSteve’s forced resignation,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2216720,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brian Niccol was announced as Chipotle’s new CEO."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2220080,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Leadership transitions at Fortune 500 \ncompanies generally span six to twelve months."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2224960,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In contrast, Chipotle’s search was \nextraordinarily short, lasting just 76 days."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2229840,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brian uniquely embodied the \nfast-food rigor, digital expertise,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2233920,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and ruthless mentality that \nAckman wanted for Chipotle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2237200,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was also extroverted, media-trained, \nand understood the value of visibility,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2241680,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "publicity, and social media - things that \nSteve never embraced. Most important of all,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2246560,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he was a proven value extractor \nwho would prioritize shareholders,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2250080,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hit the biggest numbers, and stay \nloyal to the man who appointed him."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2253680,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Ackman’s view, Taco Bell, under Brian, \nhad achieved everything that Chipotle lacked."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2258640,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The discount chain had become a \ncultural engine - launching breakfast,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2262400,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pioneering mobile ordering, \ndriving app engagement,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2265440,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and extracting maximum spend through \nengineered scarcity of beloved products."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2270000,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brian, in short, was the perfect candidate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2272240,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He set fire to the past immediately, moving \nChipotle’s headquarters to Southern California  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2276960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even though the company under Steve had just \nsigned a 15 year lease in downtown Denver."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2281440,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Employees who had been with Chipotle since \nthe 90s were effectively purged as most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2285920,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simply could not afford to suddenly uproot \ntheir lives or relocate to Orange County."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2290480,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The long-maligned CMO was finally fired."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2293440,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He also put a permanent end to the platform \nvision, shuttering Pizzeria Locale, Shophouse,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2298640,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Tasty Made - Steve's latest burger \nconcept - for dragging down the bottom line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2303760,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In his first appearance, Brian promised \n$10 billion in annual revenue, more than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2308320,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "double existing sales, 5,000 stores nationwide, \nnearly twice the company’s current footprint,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2313680,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and an additional one million \ndollars in average unit volume."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2317200,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "His agenda was clear: he was there to slash, burn, \nand squeeze every last bit of growth and profit as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2323040,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quickly as possible, even if it meant accelerating \nthe company toward saturation and commoditization."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2328800,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Initially, Brian was eager to bring over elements \nfrom Taco Bell. He teased upcoming innovations  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2333760,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like nachos, Mexican chocolate milkshakes, and \navocado tostadas as modern takes on a legacy menu."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2340240,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet all of these items were quietly \nabandoned as quickly as they appeared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2344080,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman had chosen Brian to optimize, not reinvent,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2346960,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the business. These new items would only slow \nthe line, lower sales, and reduce margin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2352240,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even nachos, which tested well, \nwere scrapped simply because they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2355600,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cannibalized sales from the \nhigher-margin burrito bowls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2358800,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brian quickly fell in line with \nAckman's mandate. Nothing should  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2361840,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ever interfere with throughput or \nthe economics of the core business."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2365520,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why Chipotle moved so quickly \nto restrict the viral quesadilla as a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2369600,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "digital-only offering, rather than \nfully integrate it into the menu."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2373440,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While this was publicly framed for convenience,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2375600,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was in reality designed to \npush more customers onto the app,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2378960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shift more sales towards higher-margin digital \norders, and protect the main assembly line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2383760,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In lieu of menu innovation, Chipotle under Brian  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2386640,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simply rearranged existing ingredients into \n\"new products\" like keto and paleo bowls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2391760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Limited-time proteins such as carne asada \nand brisket served a similar purpose."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2396480,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While marketed as exciting new additions,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2398640,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they all function primarily as promotional \nvehicles designed to increase check sizes,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2403600,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "manufacture artificial scarcity, and spike \nsales whenever they rotate onto the menu."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2408400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since every new item is an upcharge, the \ncompany's profit margins remain insulated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2413120,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For what Chipotle saved in \nR\u0026D, they blew on marketing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2416480,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They poured money into advertising and \npublicity stunts that would have been  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2419920,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unimaginable under Steve—sponsoring esports teams,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2423520,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "embedding in video game tournaments, \npaying streamers to eat on camera,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2427280,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and pushing gimmicky merchandise—all just to keep \nthe chain constantly top of mind for millennials."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2432640,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By 2020, Brian’s innovations \nwere purely operational."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2436160,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pickup shelves were installed \ninside every location so mobile  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2439440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "customers could grab their orders without \ninterrupting the in-store assembly line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2443760,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cost consultants were hired to \nanalyze how much prices could be  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2446800,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "raised in every neighborhood without \nlosing sales or triggering headlines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2451120,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While Steve had historically only raised prices \nwhen necessary, Chipotle now runs on continuous,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2456320,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "semi-annual, and tiny price increases \nstore-by-store and item-by-item by zip code."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2461600,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The company also clamped down on \nserving sizes for the first time ever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2465360,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Managers are now evaluated not only on P\u0026L \nand food safety, but also on portion control."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2471040,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every night, a system at HQ automatically \ncalculates how much food a location should  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2475440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have used based on sales, and compares it \nagainst how much inventory actually disappeared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2480240,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Any store found giving away too much chicken,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2482800,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "steak, cheese, or guacamole \ngets flagged and audited."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2485920,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This, in turn, has led to the present-day \ndynamic in which managers scrutinize workers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2490320,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with food scales and discipline those \nwho over-portion in order to protect  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2494160,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their own bonuses - and those same workers \nunder-portion customers to keep their jobs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2498960,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By 2020, Brian had delivered the ruthless \noptimization that Ackman wanted with digital  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2504000,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "orders making up nearly $3B in sales \nfor the first time in company history."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2509280,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle’s stock surged to all-time-highs, driven \nby the landmark results and management aggression."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2515040,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nothing was off limits for Brian. He raised \nthe store target from 5,000 to 6,000,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2520000,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "incorporated drive-thrus to new locations, \nand pursued expansion across middle America  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2524960,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in towns as small as 40,000 people \nunder the sole pursuit of growth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2529200,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman’s stake had more than \ntripled in under 2 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2532320,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By 2023, Brian was habitually \nraising the goalposts with little  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2536160,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "regard for the long-term health of the company."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2538400,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He promised 25% profit margins and achieved  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2541280,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it through 15% price hikes and \neven stricter portion control."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2545360,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He proclaimed that the average store would  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2547280,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "soon gross 4 million dollars a \nyear off the exact same tactics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2551040,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In his own words, the next Chipotle was Chipotle  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2553680,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "itself and that the business could \ncompound growth through scale alone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2557520,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Shareholders lapped up his story as \nBrian continued to serve them above all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2561680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He talked up dystopian innovations like \nthe implementation of cameras and AI as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2566320,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "automated surveillance systems to flag \nover-portioning along with replacement  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2570240,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "robot dispensers programmed to dump \nthe correct serving size every time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2574240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For customers, his only major announcement was \nrenaming “barbacoa” as “braised beef barbacoa.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2579280,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ultimately, Chipotle would never \nsustain the trajectory that Brian  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2582560,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had promised as most of the growth was engineered."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2585200,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet Brian and Ackman would both eventually leave \nthe company just as customers began pushing back  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2589920,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "against the nickel-and-diming that had become \ninstitutionalized over the past six years.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2594640,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They never planned to stick around long enough \nto bear the consequences of their decisions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2598800,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brian’s initial response to the portion \ncontroversy only enraged customers,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2602960,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the unexpected scale and intensity of their \nblowback signaled to him it was time to jump ship."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2608400,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He repeatedly dismissed claims \nthat portion sizes had changed,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2611760,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "insisting it was unnecessary to \nvideotape workers and recommending  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2615120,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that customers give employees a simple \nnod or a look if they wanted more food."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2619760,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But by mid-2024, the social media \ncriticism had evolved into a material  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2624240,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sales slump as Chipotle posted the first \nnegative same-store sales in a decade."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2628880,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rather than adjust the policies \nthat had created this problem,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2631840,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brian settled for a band-aid. He budgeted \nan additional $100 million dollars in food  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2636480,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "costs and sacrificed half a point of profit \nto temporarily increase portion sizes for all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2641440,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in reality, Brian was already \none foot out the door. As CEO,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2645200,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he saw the numbers before anyone else \nand knew he had squeezed the lemon dry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2649360,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chipotle under his watch was becoming \nincreasingly oversaturated, overpriced, and stale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2655120,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every store was operating at record speed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2657440,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The menu and ingredients had all been streamlined \ndown to the cheapest and most efficient variant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2662320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While Steve had worn high food costs as a \nbadge of honor and proof of ingredient quality,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2666880,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brian had hammered down food costs down \nto a record low of 29% - a reduction only  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2672160,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "possible at scale with aggressive price hikes, \nportion control, and lower quality ingredients."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2677680,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Digital ordering had matured at 35% of sales."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2680800,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The limited-time proteins had \nbecome predictable rotations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2684160,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there were now too many stores \nas every new location was starting  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2687520,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to cannibalize sales from existing ones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2689840,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only growth lever Brian hadn’t tried \nwas true menu innovation, yet that was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2694000,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now fundamentally incompatible \nwith the company he had built."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2697280,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The talent, muscle, and creativity needed to \nachieve that kind of innovation had all been  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2702240,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eradicated under Ackman’s earlier purges."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2704720,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If Brian was to sustain Chipotle’s valuation, \nhe would have to pursue much harder and riskier  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2709920,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "opportunities like international expansion \nand labor automation - initiatives that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2714320,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would require significant capital \nexpenditures and years of investment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2718160,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In short, there was nothing left to optimize  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2720160,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the short-term and nowhere \nfor the stock to go but down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2723680,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ackman also saw the writing on the wall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2725760,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The hyper-growth he had architected \nhad reached its natural conclusion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2729360,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He made no effort to persuade Brian to stay, \nnor did he care about Chipotle’s next chapter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2734240,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With the easy money gone and margins \nsqueezed to the point of customer resentment,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2738240,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "his hedge fund had extracted all the \nvalue that Chipotle had to offer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2742000,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the time of Brian’s resignation, Ackman \nhad already sold off 85% of his position."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2746880,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of those shares, 22% were sold \nat all-time highs just weeks  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2750720,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before Chipotle’s stock started tumbling \ndown on the news of Brian's departure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2755040,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The timing of both exits was \nno coincidence and Ackman’s  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2758160,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sell-off in particular is suspiciously well-timed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2761200,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ultimately, Pershing Square would exit Chipotle  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2763760,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with nearly $7 billion in profit \noff its $1.2 billion investment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2768320,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like Brian before him, Chipotle’s latest CEO can \nonly keep playing the same tune for shareholders,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2773520,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "framing operational upgrades like \nlarger rice cookers, faster grills,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2777440,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and prep robots as “innovations” that improve \nmargins but do little to restore demand."
    } ]
  } ]
}
